From 70a3e31a019836235ef5ec6245bda7798db3ea12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab bring-up <local@invalid>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:39:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kebab: pin CCI1 clock rate to 37.5MHz for correct I2C SCL
 timing

qcom,sm8250-cci is CCI v2 hardware (cci_v2_data), whose SCL timing table
is hardcoded assuming a 37.5MHz CCI clock. Upstream sm8250.dtsi never
sets assigned-clock-rates for CAM_CC_CCI_1_CLK, leaving the rate to
RCG/bootloader defaults. Live debugfs on kebab confirms cam_cc_cci_1_clk
and cam_cc_cci_1_clk_src both resting at 19.2MHz -- roughly half the
rate the driver's timing table assumes, producing out-of-spec SCL
timing on cci1 (CCI1_I2C0 / CCI1_I2C1).

This explains the front camera (IMX471 on cci1_i2c0) symptom: the
EEPROM (lenient timing tolerance) ACKs fine, but the IMX471 sensor
itself NACKs -- consistent with marginal/out-of-spec bus timing rather
than a wiring or hardware fault.

Mirrors the upstream sm8650 fix (commit 2cc1076501887746f20bdcca40ae703c8c13bc7a,
'arm64: dts: qcom: sm8650: Assign CCI clock rates to 37.5MHz', queued
linux-next 2026-08-03), where CCI maintainer Loic Poulain confirmed
37.5MHz is the correct rate for fast-mode-plus (1MHz) I2C operation on
this CCI hardware generation.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
index 949cf5197..ad2068ad1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
@@ -1960,6 +1960,9 @@ &cci0 {
 
 &cci1 {
 	status = "okay";
+
+	assigned-clocks = <&camcc CAM_CC_CCI_1_CLK>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <37500000>;
 };
 
 /*
